== WHAT `src[0].dtype` IS FOR EACH BODY -- THE FIELD ops.py:130 ACTUALLY READS
CUSTOM_FUNCTION body       dtype=!! AttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'dtype' _shape=!! AttributeError ranges=[]
CONST body                 dtype=dtypes.weakint                                       _shape=()         ranges=[]

== SO: `CallInfo.dtype` IS NOT AN UPSTREAM FIELD AT ALL.
   `repr` of the fixture's arg: (None, False, False, dtypes.i32)
   upstream's CallInfo is `CallInfo(grad_fxn, name, precompile, precompile_backward, aux)`,
   so the fixture's 4-tuple IS upstream's arg and its third element is `precompile`.
